      "id": 15,
      "name": "Collaborative AI Sandboxes for Geographically Segregated Acquisition Teams",
      "description": "The Problem: Department of War (DoW) Multi-Functional Teams (MFTs) are highly fragmented and geographically separated (e.g., AMIC HQ at JBLE, Det 2 at JBSA, OLs, and OSD partners). Acquisition, surveillance, and financial data live in deep, disconnected legacy silos (CON-IT, DEAMS, WAWF, and PMO spreadsheets). Currently, enterprise AI tools (like GenAI Gemini) lack native, live DAF365 or SharePoint connectors. This forces individual users into manual \"Doc Import\" (drag-and-drop) workflows in isolated chat sessions, making real-time, cross-echelon collaborative AI operations impossible.\nThe Solution: Establish an interim, collaborative \"AI Data Sandbox\" utilizing Google NotebookLM (or the GenAI.mil Notebook platform) to serve as a shared semantic and data-broker layer. By standardizing structured, non-proprietary data exports (exports of contract modifications, DEAMS ledgers, risk registers, and surveillance logs) and loading them into a shared, live Notebook workspace, geographically segregated MFTs can immediately collaborate in a unified, interactive AI environment. This bypasses connection delays, breaks down local data silos, and demonstrates the \"art of the possible\" for federated multi-agent decision support ahead of formal system-to-system API integration.",
      "requirements": "Collaboration & Access: Geographically separated users must be able to securely access, view, and query the same shared AI Notebook workspace simultaneously.\nSilo Elimination: The platform must support multi-format data ingestion (PDF, TXT, CSV, and Google Docs/Slides) to synthesize disparate financial, schedule, quality, and risk data into a single, unified operating picture.\nDeterministic Grounding: AI responses must be strictly bounded to the uploaded source data, featuring dynamic citations that link directly to specific pages or ledger rows (zero-hallucination guardrails).\nMulti-Tiered Views: The workspace must support three operational perspectives: Enterprise-level portfolio burndown, Division-level metrics, and individual program-level tracking.\nHuman-in-Command (HIC) Compliance: The system must act as an analytical and drafting co-pilot, leaving 100% of final approvals and statutory decisions to the human team.",
      "expected_deliverables": "A Live, Collaborative AI Workspace: A fully populated, shared Notebook sandbox containing simulated, multi-source acquisition files (simulated DEAMS ledger data, WAWF invoices, PWS requirements, and risk registers).\nStandardized Data Product Schemas: Reusable templates (JSON, CSV) that users can immediately use to export data from legacy systems and import into the shared sandbox, eliminating manual data-cleansing.\nDemonstrated Multi-Functional Workflows: Live, recorded walk-throughs of a geographically separated MFT (e.g., a Contracting Officer in Virginia and a PM in Texas) collaborating within the same workspace to:\nPerform real-time contract financial reconciliation (spotting burn rates, UOOs, and vacancy credits).\nExecute automated performance-risk monitoring (cross-referencing surveillance reports against PWS milestones).\nConduct real-time, collaborative Risk, Issue, and Opportunity (RIO) trend analysis across enterprise, division, and program levels.",
