      "id": 25,
      "name": "DoW Web Application Standard Tools",
      "description": "Virtually all DoW/USN web applications are currently hosted or planned to migrate to commercial cloud platforms with cybersecurity policy requiring CAC-PKI authentication for all users to access those applications. There are two major problems with the current situation, the first is that application configurations within cloud environments such as Amazon Web Services (AWS) are not consistently scanned for security vulnerabilities within the configuration of overlapping security policies. The only known compliance guidance is the Cloud Computing Security Requirements Guide (SRG), but no compliance tool exists for scanning for items listed in the “guide.” Furthermore, problems such as overlapping identity and access control policies consist of many lines of JSON code which, while human-readable, does not readily identify inconsistencies or problematic policies within the complex policies. Given access to frontier AI coding models without the severe restrictions levied by genai.mil would enable software development of a scanning agent or standalone tool for identifying departures from CIS-benchmark configurations or insecure policies and better secure every web application used by the DoW. Relatedly, development of a “standard” CAC-PKI authentication tool or library that all web application developers could use would rapidly assist DevOps projects across the board who all face the same problems with integrating a complex CAC-PKI authentication protocol with any new or existing web applications. Every web application, touched by every sailor would stand to gain improvements to security configuration or faster, standardized user authentication workflows.",
