      "name": "Enterprise BSO Customer Service and Intelligent Ticket Management System",
      "description": "",
      "requirements": "Develop a centralized, web-based Enterprise Customer Service and Ticket Management System to streamline the intake, assignment, tracking, escalation, and resolution of customer service requests submitted by Department of the Navy (DON) Budget Submitting Offices (BSOs).\n\nThe proposed solution should incorporate the following capabilities:\n\nCentralized Customer Service Portal: Establish a single point of entry for BSOs to submit inquiries and requests across financial management, audit readiness, manpower, budget execution, funding, administrative support, systems access, and other functional areas.\n\nAutomated Ticket Generation: Assign unique tracking numbers to submitted requests and capture relevant information, including requesting organization, request category, description, priority, submission date, and supporting documentation.\n\nIntelligent Request Classification and Routing: Leverage rules-based automation and, where authorized, artificial intelligence to classify requests and recommend the appropriate functional support team based on the nature of the inquiry.\n\nWorkflow Management: Enable designated personnel to assign, reassign, prioritize, escalate, and resolve requests while maintaining accountability and visibility throughout the ticket lifecycle.\n\nCustomer Status Tracking: Provide BSOs with real-time visibility into request status, assigned support organization, outstanding actions, and resolution progress.\n\nAutomated Notifications: Generate acknowledgments, status updates, requests for additional information, and escalation notifications.\n\nKnowledge Management: Establish a centralized repository of frequently asked questions, standardized procedures, recurring issues, and documented resolutions.\n\nExecutive Reporting and Analytics: Develop interactive dashboards displaying ticket volumes, resolution timelines, workload distribution, recurring issues, customer satisfaction, and performance against established service-level targets.\n\nSecurity and Compliance: Incorporate role-based access controls, audit trails, data protection, records retention, and applicable DON/DoD cybersecurity requirements.\n\nScalability and Integration: Design the solution to accommodate additional BSOs, functional organizations, service categories, and integration with approved enterprise platforms.",
      "expected_deliverables": "Deliverable 1: Functional Prototype\n\nA working, web-based demonstration of the Enterprise BSO Customer Service Portal, allowing users to submit, categorize, assign, track, and resolve customer service requests.\n\nDeliverable 2: Automated Ticket Management Workflow\n\nA configurable workflow supporting unique ticket generation, request classification, functional routing, ownership assignment, status updates, escalation, and closure.\n\nDeliverable 3: BSO Customer Interface\n\nAn intuitive, user-friendly interface through which BSO representatives can submit service requests, review existing tickets, provide additional information, and monitor resolution progress.\n\nDeliverable 4: Functional Support Workspace\n\nA centralized workspace enabling support teams to manage assigned tickets, collaborate across functional areas, document actions, and communicate resolutions.\n\nDeliverable 5: Executive Performance Dashboard\n\nAn interactive reporting dashboard providing leadership with visibility into request volumes, open and overdue tickets, response and resolution times, functional workload, service trends, and customer satisfaction.\n\nDeliverable 6: Knowledge Management Repository\n\nA searchable repository of frequently asked questions, standard operating procedures, common issues, and previously documented resolutions to support self-service and reduce repetitive inquiries.\n\nDeliverable 7: Business Requirements and Governance Documentation\n\nDocumentation outlining system requirements, functional responsibilities, workflow procedures, security considerations, performance measures, and recommended governance structure.\n\nDeliverable 8: Pilot Evaluation and Implementation Roadmap\n\nA pilot demonstration involving selected BSOs and functional support organizations, followed by an assessment of usability, routing accuracy, operational effectiveness, and recommendations for phased enterprise implementation.\n\nExpected Operational Outcomes\n\nImproved responsiveness and accountability for BSO customer service requests.\n\nReduced reliance on fragmented email correspondence and informal tracking mechanisms.\n\nIncreased transparency into request ownership, status, and resolution.\n\nStandardized customer service processes across functional organizations.\n\nEnhanced leadership visibility into support requirements and resource demands.\n\nImproved identification of recurring issues, process inefficiencies, and training opportunities.\n\nA scalable foundation for enterprise-wide customer service management across the Department of the Navy.",
